-- ccc21-part-19.l4 -- PART XIX, Indictable Offences -- Trial Without Jury, ss 554 to 572 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (sections 552 and 553 are in ccc21-part-19-absolute.l4).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Imports the keel's core, this part's nouns, ss 552-553, and Part XVIII (the helpers for "14 years or more" and the answers of the election).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words: each such branch carries `-- FALSE-kind (...): "<quote>"`); NOTHING (not covered: `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`).
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. `-- GRANT-GATE: ...` and `-- CLAIM-NAMED` mark the groups NOTES.md counts for a lawyer (see ccc21-part-17.l4's header).
-- Seams this part takes as inputs: `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` and `s 577 a direct indictment has been preferred` (MAYBE BOOLEAN, carried through as NOTHING when NOTHING),
-- `s 2 organization: the accused is an organization` (MAYBE BOOLEAN). Time is taken in whole days: a date is a day, and "the 60th day following" is the completion date plus 60 days.

§ `PART XIX -- Indictable Offences -- Trial Without Jury`

§§ `Sections 554 to 557 -- Jurisdiction of provincial court judges`

-- 554 (1) Subject to subsection (2), if an accused is charged in an information with an indictable offence other than an offence that is mentioned in section 469, and the offence is not one over which a provincial court judge has absolute jurisdiction
-- under section 553, a provincial court judge may try the accused if the accused elects to be tried by a provincial court judge.
-- src:12263 | 554 (1) Subject to subsection (2), if an accused is charged in an information with an indictable offence other than an offence that is mentioned in section 469, and the offence is not one over which a provincial court judge has absolute jurisdiction under section 553, a provincial court judge may try the accused if the accused elects to be tried by a provincial court judge.
@ref s 554(1) (src:12263-12263)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 535 the charge`
      `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the accused's answer` IS A `s 536(2) the accused's answer when put to an election`
      `the proceedings are criminal proceedings in Nunavut` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 554(1) a provincial court judge may try the accused` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the proceedings are criminal proceedings in Nunavut` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection (2)"
        IF NOT charge's `s 535 the facts that bear on absolute jurisdiction`'s `s 553 the accused is charged in an information` THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if an accused is charged in an information"
        IF NOT `s 535 the offence charged is an indictable offence` charge THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with an indictable offence"
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "other than an offence that is mentioned in section 469"
        IF `s 553 the offence is within the absolute jurisdiction of a provincial court judge` (charge's `s 535 the facts that bear on absolute jurisdiction`) EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the offence is not one over which a provincial court judge has absolute jurisdiction under section 553"
        IF NOT `s 536(3) the accused elects to be tried by a provincial court judge` `the accused's answer` THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the accused elects to be tried by a provincial court judge"
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is mentioned in section 469 is for that section
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 554 (2) With respect to criminal proceedings in Nunavut, if an accused is charged in an information with an indictable offence other than an offence that is mentioned in section 469 and the offence is not one over which a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice
-- has absolute jurisdiction under section 553, a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may try the accused if the accused elects to be tried by a judge without a jury.
