-- 555 (2) If an accused is before a provincial court judge, charged with an offence prosecuted by indictment mentioned in paragraph 553(a) or subparagraph 553(b)(i), and, at any time before the provincial court judge makes an adjudication, the evidence
-- establishes that the subject matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument or that its value exceeds $5,000, the provincial court judge shall put the accused to their election in accordance with subsection 536(2.1).
-- src:12274 | (2) If an accused is before a provincial court judge, charged with an offence prosecuted by indictment mentioned in paragraph 553(a) or subparagraph 553(b)(i), and, at any time before the provincial court judge makes an adjudication, the evidence establishes that the subject matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument or that its value exceeds $5,000, the provincial court judge shall put the accused to their election in accordance with subsection 536(2.1).
@ref s 555(2) (src:12274-12274)
GIVEN `an accused is before a provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence charged, as paragraph (a) names it` IS A `s 553(a) the offence charged, as paragraph (a) names it`
      `the offence is prosecuted by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provincial court judge has made an adjudication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence establishes that the subject matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument or that its value exceeds 5,000 dollars` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 555(2) the provincial court judge shall put the accused to their election in accordance with subsection 536(2.1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an accused is before a provincial court judge` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an accused is before a provincial court judge"
        IF `the offence charged, as paragraph (a) names it` EQUALS `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "charged with an offence prosecuted by indictment mentioned in paragraph 553(a) or subparagraph 553(b)(i)"
        IF NOT `the offence is prosecuted by indictment` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "charged with an offence prosecuted by indictment"
        IF `the provincial court judge has made an adjudication` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time before the provincial court judge makes an adjudication"
        IF NOT `the evidence establishes that the subject matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument or that its value exceeds 5,000 dollars` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the evidence establishes that the subject matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument or that its value exceeds $5,000"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 555 (3) If an accused is put to their election under subsection (1.1) or (2), the following provisions apply: (a) if the accused elects to be tried by a judge without a jury or a court composed of a judge and jury or does not elect when put to their election,
-- the provincial court judge shall endorse on the information a record of the nature of the election or deemed election; and (b) if the accused elects to be tried by a provincial court judge, the provincial court judge shall endorse on the information a record of the election and continue with the trial.
