§§ `Sections 558 and 559 -- Judge's jurisdiction with consent`

-- 558 If an accused who is charged with an indictable offence, other than an offence mentioned in section 469, elects under section 536 or 536.1 or re-elects under section 561 or 561.1 to be tried by a judge without a jury, the accused shall,
-- subject to this Part, be tried by a judge without a jury.
-- src:12309 | 558 If an accused who is charged with an indictable offence, other than an offence mentioned in section 469, elects under section 536 or 536.1 or re-elects under section 561 or 561.1 to be tried by a judge without a jury, the accused shall, subject to this Part, be tried by a judge without a jury.
@ref s 558 (src:12309-12309)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 535 the charge`
      `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the accused elects under section 536 or 536.1 or re-elects under section 561 or 561.1 to be tried by a judge without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another provision of this Part displaces the election` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 558 the accused shall be tried by a judge without a jury` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `s 535 the offence charged is an indictable offence` charge THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an accused who is charged with an indictable offence"
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than an offence mentioned in section 469"
        IF NOT `the accused elects under section 536 or 536.1 or re-elects under section 561 or 561.1 to be tried by a judge without a jury` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "elects under section 536 or 536.1 or re-elects under section 561 or 561.1 to be tried by a judge without a jury"
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is mentioned in section 469 is for that section
        IF `another provision of this Part displaces the election` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to this Part"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 559 (1) A judge who holds a trial under this Part shall, for all purposes thereof and proceedings connected therewith or relating thereto, be a court of record.
-- src:12311 | 559 (1) A judge who holds a trial under this Part shall, for all purposes thereof and proceedings connected therewith or relating thereto, be a court of record.
