§§ `Section 561 -- Right to re-elect`

-- The facts a re-election turns on, for one accused: the mode they elected (or are deemed to have elected), the mode they now wish to re-elect, whether they are entitled to request a preliminary inquiry and whether one was requested
-- under subsection 536(4), the date it was completed (NOTHING: it has not been), the date of the re-election, the day first appointed for the trial, and whether the prosecutor has consented in writing. A day is a whole calendar day.
-- src:12331 | 561 (1) An accused who elects or is deemed to have elected a mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge may re-elect,
-- src:12332 | (a) if the accused is charged with an offence for which a preliminary inquiry has been requested under subsection 536(4),
-- src:12333 | (i) at any time before or after the completion of the preliminary inquiry, with the written consent of the prosecutor, to be tried by a provincial court judge,
-- src:12334 | (ii) at any time before the completion of the preliminary inquiry or before the 60th day following the completion of the preliminary inquiry, as of right, another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, and
-- src:12335 | (iii) on or after the 60th day following the completion of the preliminary inquiry, any mode of trial with the written consent of the prosecutor; or
-- src:12336 | (b) if the accused is charged with an offence for which they are not entitled to request a preliminary inquiry or if they did not request a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536(4),
-- src:12337 | (i) as of right, not later than 60 days before the day first appointed for the trial, another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, or
-- src:12338 | (ii) any mode of trial with the written consent of the prosecutor.
@ref s 561(1) (src:12331-12338)
DECLARE `s 561 the re-election facts` HAS
    `s 561 the mode elected or deemed elected` IS A `s 536(2) mode of trial`
    `s 561 the mode the accused wishes to re-elect` IS A `s 536(2) mode of trial`
    `s 561 the accused is entitled to request a preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 561 a preliminary inquiry has been requested under subsection 536(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 561 the date the preliminary inquiry was completed` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `s 561 the date of the re-election` IS A DATE
    `s 561 the day first appointed for the trial` IS A DATE
    `s 561 the prosecutor has consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:12331 | 561 (1) An accused who elects or is deemed to have elected a mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge may re-elect,
-- src:12332 | (a) if the accused is charged with an offence for which a preliminary inquiry has been requested under subsection 536(4),
-- src:12333 | (i) at any time before or after the completion of the preliminary inquiry, with the written consent of the prosecutor, to be tried by a provincial court judge,
-- src:12334 | (ii) at any time before the completion of the preliminary inquiry or before the 60th day following the completion of the preliminary inquiry, as of right, another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, and
-- src:12335 | (iii) on or after the 60th day following the completion of the preliminary inquiry, any mode of trial with the written consent of the prosecutor; or
-- src:12336 | (b) if the accused is charged with an offence for which they are not entitled to request a preliminary inquiry or if they did not request a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536(4),
-- src:12337 | (i) as of right, not later than 60 days before the day first appointed for the trial, another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, or
-- src:12338 | (ii) any mode of trial with the written consent of the prosecutor.
@ref s 561(1) (src:12331-12338)
DECLARE `s 561 the basis on which the accused may re-elect` IS ONE OF
    `s 561 as of right`
    `s 561 only with the written consent of the prosecutor`

-- 561 (1) An accused who elects or is deemed to have elected a mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge may re-elect, (a) if the accused is charged with an offence for which a preliminary inquiry has been requested under subsection 536(4),
-- (i) at any time before or after the completion of the preliminary inquiry, with the written consent of the prosecutor, to be tried by a provincial court judge,
-- src:12331 | 561 (1) An accused who elects or is deemed to have elected a mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge may re-elect,
-- src:12332 | (a) if the accused is charged with an offence for which a preliminary inquiry has been requested under subsection 536(4),
-- src:12333 | (i) at any time before or after the completion of the preliminary inquiry, with the written consent of the prosecutor, to be tried by a provincial court judge,
@ref s 561(1)(a)(i) (src:12331-12333)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 561 the re-election facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 561(1)(a)(i) the accused may re-elect to be tried by a provincial court judge, with the written consent of the prosecutor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF facts's `s 561 the mode elected or deemed elected` EQUALS `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An accused who elects or is deemed to have elected a mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge may re-elect"
        IF NOT facts's `s 561 a preliminary inquiry has been requested under subsection 536(4)` THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the accused is charged with an offence for which a preliminary inquiry has been requested under subsection 536(4)"
        IF NOT (facts's `s 561 the mode the accused wishes to re-elect` EQUALS `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to be tried by a provincial court judge"
        IF NOT facts's `s 561 the prosecutor has consented in writing` THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with the written consent of the prosecutor"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (ii) at any time before the completion of the preliminary inquiry or before the 60th day following the completion of the preliminary inquiry, as of right, another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, and
-- src:12334 | (ii) at any time before the completion of the preliminary inquiry or before the 60th day following the completion of the preliminary inquiry, as of right, another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, and
@ref s 561(1)(a)(ii) (src:12334-12334)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 561 the re-election facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 561(1)(a)(ii) the accused may re-elect another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, as of right` MEANS   -- CLAIM-NAMED
    BRANCH
        IF facts's `s 561 the mode elected or deemed elected` EQUALS `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An accused who elects or is deemed to have elected a mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge may re-elect"
        IF NOT facts's `s 561 a preliminary inquiry has been requested under subsection 536(4)` THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the accused is charged with an offence for which a preliminary inquiry has been requested under subsection 536(4)"
        IF facts's `s 561 the mode the accused wishes to re-elect` EQUALS `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge` OR facts's `s 561 the mode the accused wishes to re-elect` EQUALS facts's `s 561 the mode elected or deemed elected` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge"
        IF `the 60th day following the completion has been reached` THEN JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before the 60th day following the completion of the preliminary inquiry"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the 60th day following the completion has been reached` MEANS
            CONSIDER facts's `s 561 the date the preliminary inquiry was completed`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST completed THEN Day (facts's `s 561 the date of the re-election`) AT LEAST (Day completed PLUS 60)

-- (iii) on or after the 60th day following the completion of the preliminary inquiry, any mode of trial with the written consent of the prosecutor; or
-- src:12335 | (iii) on or after the 60th day following the completion of the preliminary inquiry, any mode of trial with the written consent of the prosecutor; or
@ref s 561(1)(a)(iii) (src:12335-12335)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 561 the re-election facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 561(1)(a)(iii) the accused may re-elect any mode of trial, with the written consent of the prosecutor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF facts's `s 561 the mode elected or deemed elected` EQUALS `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An accused who elects or is deemed to have elected a mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge may re-elect"
        IF NOT facts's `s 561 a preliminary inquiry has been requested under subsection 536(4)` THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the accused is charged with an offence for which a preliminary inquiry has been requested under subsection 536(4)"
        IF NOT `the 60th day following the completion has been reached` THEN JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on or after the 60th day following the completion of the preliminary inquiry"
        IF NOT facts's `s 561 the prosecutor has consented in writing` THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with the written consent of the prosecutor"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the 60th day following the completion has been reached` MEANS
            CONSIDER facts's `s 561 the date the preliminary inquiry was completed`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST completed THEN Day (facts's `s 561 the date of the re-election`) AT LEAST (Day completed PLUS 60)

