§§ `Section 561.1 -- Right to re-elect -- Nunavut`

-- 561.1 (1) An accused who has elected or is deemed to have elected a mode of trial may re-elect any other mode of trial at any time with the written consent of the prosecutor.
-- src:12360 | 561.1 (1) An accused who has elected or is deemed to have elected a mode of trial may re-elect any other mode of trial at any time with the written consent of the prosecutor.
@ref s 561.1(1) (src:12360-12360)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 561 the re-election facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 561.1(1) the accused may re-elect any other mode of trial, with the written consent of the prosecutor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF facts's `s 561 the mode the accused wishes to re-elect` EQUALS facts's `s 561 the mode elected or deemed elected` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "re-elect any other mode of trial"
        IF NOT facts's `s 561 the prosecutor has consented in writing` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with the written consent of the prosecutor"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 561.1 (2) An accused who has elected or is deemed to have elected a mode of trial but has not requested a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3) or is not entitled to make such a request under that subsection may, as of right, re-elect to be tried by any other mode of trial
-- at any time up to 60 days before the day first appointed for the trial.
-- src:12362 | (2) An accused who has elected or is deemed to have elected a mode of trial but has not requested a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3) or is not entitled to make such a request under that subsection may, as of right, re-elect to be tried by any other mode of trial at any time up to 60 days before the day first appointed for the trial.
@ref s 561.1(2) (src:12362-12362)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 561 the re-election facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 561.1(2) the accused may re-elect to be tried by any other mode of trial, as of right` MEANS   -- CLAIM-NAMED
    BRANCH
        IF facts's `s 561 the accused is entitled to request a preliminary inquiry` AND facts's `s 561 a preliminary inquiry has been requested under subsection 536(4)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "but has not requested a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3) or is not entitled to make such a request under that subsection"
        IF facts's `s 561 the mode the accused wishes to re-elect` EQUALS facts's `s 561 the mode elected or deemed elected` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "re-elect to be tried by any other mode of trial"
        IF (Day (facts's `s 561 the day first appointed for the trial`) MINUS Day (facts's `s 561 the date of the re-election`)) LESS THAN 60 THEN JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time up to 60 days before the day first appointed for the trial"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 561.1 (3) An accused who has elected or is deemed to have elected a mode of trial and has requested a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3) may, as of right, re-elect to be tried by the other mode of trial at any time before the completion of the preliminary inquiry
-- or before the 60th day after its completion.
-- src:12364 | (3) An accused who has elected or is deemed to have elected a mode of trial and has requested a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3) may, as of right, re-elect to be tried by the other mode of trial at any time before the completion of the preliminary inquiry or before the 60th day after its completion.
@ref s 561.1(3) (src:12364-12364)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 561 the re-election facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 561.1(3) the accused may re-elect to be tried by the other mode of trial, as of right` MEANS   -- CLAIM-NAMED
    BRANCH
        IF NOT facts's `s 561 a preliminary inquiry has been requested under subsection 536(4)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and has requested a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)"
        IF facts's `s 561 the mode the accused wishes to re-elect` EQUALS facts's `s 561 the mode elected or deemed elected` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "re-elect to be tried by the other mode of trial"
        IF `the 60th day after the completion has been reached` THEN JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time before the completion of the preliminary inquiry or before the 60th day after its completion"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the 60th day after the completion has been reached` MEANS
            CONSIDER facts's `s 561 the date the preliminary inquiry was completed`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST completed THEN Day (facts's `s 561 the date of the re-election`) AT LEAST (Day completed PLUS 60)

-- src:12360 | 561.1 (1) An accused who has elected or is deemed to have elected a mode of trial may re-elect any other mode of trial at any time with the written consent of the prosecutor.
-- src:12361 | Right to re-elect before trial — Nunavut
-- src:12362 | (2) An accused who has elected or is deemed to have elected a mode of trial but has not requested a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3) or is not entitled to make such a request under that subsection may, as of right, re-elect to be tried by any other mode of trial at any time up to 60 days before the day first appointed for the trial.
-- src:12363 | Right to re-elect at preliminary inquiry — Nunavut
-- src:12364 | (3) An accused who has elected or is deemed to have elected a mode of trial and has requested a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3) may, as of right, re-elect to be tried by the other mode of trial at any time before the completion of the preliminary inquiry or before the 60th day after its completion.
@ref s 561.1 (src:12360-12364)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 561 the re-election facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 561 the basis on which the accused may re-elect`
`s 561.1 the basis on which the accused may re-elect` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 561.1(2) the accused may re-elect to be tried by any other mode of trial, as of right` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 561.1(3) the accused may re-elect to be tried by the other mode of trial, as of right` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST `s 561 as of right`
        IF `s 561.1(1) the accused may re-elect any other mode of trial, with the written consent of the prosecutor` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST `s 561 only with the written consent of the prosecutor`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): no subsection of section 561.1 gives the right on these facts

-- 561.1 (4) If an accused wishes to re-elect under subsection (1) or (3), before the completion of the preliminary inquiry, the accused shall give notice in writing of the wish to re-elect, together with the written consent of the prosecutor, if that consent is required,
-- to the justice of the peace or judge presiding at the preliminary inquiry who shall on receipt of the notice put the accused to a re-election in the manner set out in subsection (9).
-- src:12366 | (4) If an accused wishes to re-elect under subsection (1) or (3), before the completion of the preliminary inquiry, the accused shall give notice in writing of the wish to re-elect, together with the written consent of the prosecutor, if that consent is required, to the justice of the peace or judge presiding at the preliminary inquiry who shall on receipt of the notice put the accused to a re-election in the manner set out in subsection (9).
