§§ `Sections 562 and 562.1 -- Proceedings following re-election`

-- 562 (1) If the accused re-elects under subparagraph 561(1)(a)(i) before the completion of the preliminary inquiry, under paragraph 561(1)(a) after the completion of the preliminary inquiry or under paragraph 561(1)(b),
-- the provincial court judge or judge, as the case may be, shall proceed with the trial or appoint a time and place for the trial.
-- src:12383 | 562 (1) If the accused re-elects under subparagraph 561(1)(a)(i) before the completion of the preliminary inquiry, under paragraph 561(1)(a) after the completion of the preliminary inquiry or under paragraph 561(1)(b), the provincial court judge or judge, as the case may be, shall proceed with the trial or appoint a time and place for the trial.
@ref s 562(1) (src:12383-12383)
GIVEN `the accused re-elects under subparagraph 561(1)(a)(i) before the completion of the preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused re-elects under paragraph 561(1)(a) after the completion of the preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused re-elects under paragraph 561(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 562(1) the provincial court judge or judge shall proceed with the trial or appoint a time and place for the trial` MEANS
    IF    `the accused re-elects under subparagraph 561(1)(a)(i) before the completion of the preliminary inquiry`
       OR `the accused re-elects under paragraph 561(1)(a) after the completion of the preliminary inquiry`
       OR `the accused re-elects under paragraph 561(1)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the accused re-elects under subparagraph 561(1)(a)(i) before the completion of the preliminary inquiry, under paragraph 561(1)(a) after the completion of the preliminary inquiry or under paragraph 561(1)(b)"

-- 562 (2) If the accused re-elects under subparagraph 561(1)(a)(ii) before the completion of the preliminary inquiry, or under subsection 561(2), and requests a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536(4), the justice shall proceed with the preliminary inquiry.
-- src:12385 | (2) If the accused re-elects under subparagraph 561(1)(a)(ii) before the completion of the preliminary inquiry, or under subsection 561(2), and requests a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536(4), the justice shall proceed with the preliminary inquiry.
@ref s 562(2) (src:12385-12385)
GIVEN `the accused re-elects under subparagraph 561(1)(a)(ii) before the completion of the preliminary inquiry, or under subsection 561(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused requests a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 562(2) the justice shall proceed with the preliminary inquiry` MEANS
    IF `the accused re-elects under subparagraph 561(1)(a)(ii) before the completion of the preliminary inquiry, or under subsection 561(2)` AND `the accused requests a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the accused re-elects under subparagraph 561(1)(a)(ii) before the completion of the preliminary inquiry, or under subsection 561(2), and requests a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536(4)"

-- 562.1 (1) If the accused re-elects under subsection 561.1(1) to be tried by a judge without a jury and does not request a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3), or if the accused re-elects any other mode of trial under subsection 561.1(2)
-- but is not entitled to make a request for a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3), the judge shall proceed with the trial or appoint a time and place for the trial.
-- src:12387 | 562.1 (1) If the accused re-elects under subsection 561.1(1) to be tried by a judge without a jury and does not request a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3), or if the accused re-elects any other mode of trial under subsection 561.1(2) but is not entitled to make a request for a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3), the judge shall proceed with the trial or appoint a time and place for the trial.
@ref s 562.1(1) (src:12387-12387)
GIVEN `the accused re-elects under subsection 561.1(1) to be tried by a judge without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused requests a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused re-elects any other mode of trial under subsection 561.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is able to make a request for a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 562.1(1) the judge shall proceed with the trial or appoint a time and place for the trial` MEANS
    IF    (`the accused re-elects under subsection 561.1(1) to be tried by a judge without a jury` AND NOT `the accused requests a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)`)
       OR (`the accused re-elects any other mode of trial under subsection 561.1(2)` AND NOT `the accused is able to make a request for a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the accused re-elects under subsection 561.1(1) to be tried by a judge without a jury and does not request a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3), or if the accused re-elects any other mode of trial under subsection 561.1(2) but is not entitled to make a request for a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)"

-- 562.1 (2) If the accused re-elects under section 561.1 before the completion of the preliminary inquiry to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury, and requests a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3),
-- the justice of the peace or judge shall proceed with the preliminary inquiry.
-- src:12389 | (2) If the accused re-elects under section 561.1 before the completion of the preliminary inquiry to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury, and requests a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3), the justice of the peace or judge shall proceed with the preliminary inquiry.
@ref s 562.1(2) (src:12389-12389)
GIVEN `the accused re-elects under section 561.1 before the completion of the preliminary inquiry to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused requests a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 562.1(2) the justice of the peace or judge shall proceed with the preliminary inquiry` MEANS
    IF `the accused re-elects under section 561.1 before the completion of the preliminary inquiry to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury` AND `the accused requests a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the accused re-elects under section 561.1 before the completion of the preliminary inquiry to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury, and requests a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)"

