§§ `Sections 563 and 563.1 -- Proceedings on re-election to be tried without jury`

-- 563 Where an accused re-elects under section 561 to be tried by a provincial court judge, (a) the accused shall be tried on the information that was before the justice at the preliminary inquiry, if applicable,
-- subject to any amendments to the information that may be allowed by the provincial court judge by whom the accused is tried; and (b) the provincial court judge before whom the re-election is made shall endorse on the information a record of the re-election.
-- src:12393 | 563 Where an accused re-elects under section 561 to be tried by a provincial court judge,
-- src:12394 | (a) the accused shall be tried on the information that was before the justice at the preliminary inquiry, if applicable, subject to any amendments to the information that may be allowed by the provincial court judge by whom the accused is tried; and
@ref s 563(a) (src:12393-12394)
GIVEN `the accused re-elects under section 561 to be tried by a provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a preliminary inquiry was held` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provincial court judge by whom the accused is tried has allowed an amendment to the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 563(a) the accused shall be tried on the information that was before the justice at the preliminary inquiry` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused re-elects under section 561 to be tried by a provincial court judge` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused re-elects under section 561 to be tried by a provincial court judge"
        IF NOT `a preliminary inquiry was held` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if applicable"
        IF `the provincial court judge by whom the accused is tried has allowed an amendment to the information` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to any amendments to the information that may be allowed by the provincial court judge by whom the accused is tried"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12393 | 563 Where an accused re-elects under section 561 to be tried by a provincial court judge,
-- src:12394 | (a) the accused shall be tried on the information that was before the justice at the preliminary inquiry, if applicable, subject to any amendments to the information that may be allowed by the provincial court judge by whom the accused is tried; and
-- src:12395 | (b) the provincial court judge before whom the re-election is made shall endorse on the information a record of the re-election.
@ref s 563(b) (src:12393-12395)
GIVEN `the accused re-elects under section 561 to be tried by a provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 563(b) the provincial court judge before whom the re-election is made shall endorse on the information a record of the re-election` MEANS
    IF `the accused re-elects under section 561 to be tried by a provincial court judge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused re-elects under section 561 to be tried by a provincial court judge"

-- 563.1 (1) If an accused re-elects under section 561.1 to be tried by a judge without a jury and does not request a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3) or is not entitled to make such a request under that subsection,
-- (a) the accused shall be tried on the information that was before the justice of the peace or judge at the preliminary inquiry, if applicable, subject to any amendments that may be allowed by the judge by whom the accused is tried; and (b) the judge before whom the re-election is made shall endorse on the information a record of the re-election.
