§§ `Section 565 -- Election deemed to have been made`

-- 565 (1) If an accused is ordered to stand trial for an offence that, under this Part, may be tried by a judge without a jury, the accused shall, for the purposes of the provisions of this Part relating to election and re-election,
-- be deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury if (a) the justice of the peace, provincial court judge or judge, as the case may be, declined to record the election or re-election of the accused under section 567 or subsection 567.1(1);
-- or (b) the accused does not elect when put to an election under section 536 or 536.1.
-- src:12404 | 565 (1) If an accused is ordered to stand trial for an offence that, under this Part, may be tried by a judge without a jury, the accused shall, for the purposes of the provisions of this Part relating to election and re-election, be deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury if
-- src:12405 | (a) the justice of the peace, provincial court judge or judge, as the case may be, declined to record the election or re-election of the accused under section 567 or subsection 567.1(1); or
-- src:12406 | (b) the accused does not elect when put to an election under section 536 or 536.1.
@ref s 565(1) (src:12404-12406)
GIVEN `the accused is ordered to stand trial for an offence that, under this Part, may be tried by a judge without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice of the peace, provincial court judge or judge declined to record the election or re-election of the accused under section 567 or subsection 567.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused was put to an election under section 536 or 536.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused's answer` IS A `s 536(2) the accused's answer when put to an election`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 565(1) the accused is deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused is ordered to stand trial for an offence that, under this Part, may be tried by a judge without a jury` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an accused is ordered to stand trial for an offence that, under this Part, may be tried by a judge without a jury"
        IF `the justice of the peace, provincial court judge or judge declined to record the election or re-election of the accused under section 567 or subsection 567.1(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the accused was put to an election under section 536 or 536.1` AND `the accused's answer` EQUALS `s 536(2) does not elect` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the justice of the peace, provincial court judge or judge, as the case may be, declined to record the election or re-election of the accused under section 567 or subsection 567.1(1); or (b) the accused does not elect when put to an election under section 536 or 536.1"

