§§ `Sections 568 and 569 -- Attorney General may require trial by jury`

-- "punishable with imprisonment for five years or less" (ss 568 and 569(1)): is the most the indictable limb allows five years or less? "Imprisonment for life" is more than five years; "five years less a day" is below five years.
-- src:12439 | 568 Even if an accused elects under section 536 or re-elects under section 561 or subsection 565(2) to be tried by a judge or provincial court judge, as the case may be, the Attorney General may require the accused to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury unless the alleged offence is one that is punishable with imprisonment for five years or less. If the Attorney General so requires, a judge or provincial court judge has no jurisdiction to try the accused under this Part and a preliminary inquiry must be held if requested under subsection 536(4), unless one has already been held or the re-election was made under subsection 565(2).
@ref s 568 (src:12439-12439)
GIVEN `the maximum imprisonment for the offence` IS AN Imprisonment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 568 an offence punishable with imprisonment for five years or less` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the maximum imprisonment for the offence`
    WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section that creates the offence states the maximum, and none is given here
    WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "punishable with imprisonment for five years or less"
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` term THEN
        IF `term is below 5 years` OR (term's years EQUALS 5 AND term's months EQUALS 0 AND term's days EQUALS 0)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "punishable with imprisonment for five years or less"
        WHERE
            `term is below 5 years` MEANS
                term's years LESS THAN 5 OR (term's years EQUALS 5 AND term's `less a day`)

-- 568 Even if an accused elects under section 536 or re-elects under section 561 or subsection 565(2) to be tried by a judge or provincial court judge, as the case may be, the Attorney General may require the accused to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury
-- unless the alleged offence is one that is punishable with imprisonment for five years or less.
-- src:12439 | 568 Even if an accused elects under section 536 or re-elects under section 561 or subsection 565(2) to be tried by a judge or provincial court judge, as the case may be, the Attorney General may require the accused to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury unless the alleged offence is one that is punishable with imprisonment for five years or less. If the Attorney General so requires, a judge or provincial court judge has no jurisdiction to try the accused under this Part and a preliminary inquiry must be held if requested under subsection 536(4), unless one has already been held or the re-election was made under subsection 565(2).
@ref s 568 (src:12439-12439)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 535 the charge`
      `the accused elected under section 536 or re-elected under section 561 or subsection 565(2) to be tried by a judge or provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 568 the Attorney General may require the accused to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused elected under section 536 or re-elected under section 561 or subsection 565(2) to be tried by a judge or provincial court judge` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Even if an accused elects under section 536 or re-elects under section 561 or subsection 565(2) to be tried by a judge or provincial court judge"
        IF `five years or less` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: closed by the text -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the alleged offence is one that is punishable with imprisonment for five years or less"
        IF `five years or less` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the maximum imprisonment for the offence is not stated
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `five years or less` MEANS `s 568 an offence punishable with imprisonment for five years or less` (charge's `s 535 the maximum imprisonment for the offence on indictment`)

-- 568 If the Attorney General so requires, a judge or provincial court judge has no jurisdiction to try the accused under this Part.
