-- 570 (4) A copy of a conviction in Form 35 or of an order in Form 36 or 37, certified by the judge or by the clerk or other proper officer of the court, or by the provincial court judge, as the case may be, or proved to be a true copy, is, on proof of the identity of the person
-- to whom the conviction or order relates, sufficient evidence in any legal proceedings to prove the conviction of that person or the making of the order against that person or his acquittal, as the case may be, for the offence mentioned in the copy of the conviction or order.
-- src:12451 | (4) A copy of a conviction in Form 35 or of an order in Form 36 or 37, certified by the judge or by the clerk or other proper officer of the court, or by the provincial court judge, as the case may be, or proved to be a true copy, is, on proof of the identity of the person to whom the conviction or order relates, sufficient evidence in any legal proceedings to prove the conviction of that person or the making of the order against that person or his acquittal, as the case may be, for the offence mentioned in the copy of the conviction or order.
@ref s 570(4) (src:12451-12451)
GIVEN `the copy is a copy of a conviction in Form 35 or of an order in Form 36 or 37` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy is certified by the judge or by the clerk or other proper officer of the court, or by the provincial court judge, or is proved to be a true copy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the identity of the person to whom the conviction or order relates is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 570(4) the copy is sufficient evidence in any legal proceedings to prove the conviction, the making of the order or the acquittal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the copy is a copy of a conviction in Form 35 or of an order in Form 36 or 37` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A copy of a conviction in Form 35 or of an order in Form 36 or 37"
        IF NOT `the copy is certified by the judge or by the clerk or other proper officer of the court, or by the provincial court judge, or is proved to be a true copy` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "certified by the judge or by the clerk or other proper officer of the court, or by the provincial court judge, as the case may be, or proved to be a true copy"
        IF NOT `the identity of the person to whom the conviction or order relates is proved` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on proof of the identity of the person to whom the conviction or order relates"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 570 (5) If an accused other than an organization is convicted, the judge or provincial court judge, as the case may be, shall issue a warrant of committal in Form 21, and section 528 applies in respect of a warrant of committal issued under this subsection.
-- src:12453 | (5) If an accused other than an organization is convicted, the judge or provincial court judge, as the case may be, shall issue a warrant of committal in Form 21, and section 528 applies in respect of a warrant of committal issued under this subsection.
@ref s 570(5) (src:12453-12453)
GIVEN `s 2 organization: the accused is an organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the accused is convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 570(5) the judge or provincial court judge shall issue a warrant of committal in Form 21` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused is convicted` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an accused other than an organization is convicted"
        IF `s 2 organization: the accused is an organization` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than an organization"
        IF `s 2 organization: the accused is an organization` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the accused is an organization is for section 2
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12453 | (5) If an accused other than an organization is convicted, the judge or provincial court judge, as the case may be, shall issue a warrant of committal in Form 21, and section 528 applies in respect of a warrant of committal issued under this subsection.
@ref s 570(5) (src:12453-12453)
GIVEN `a warrant of committal has been issued under subsection 570(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 570(5) section 528 applies in respect of the warrant of committal` MEANS
    IF `a warrant of committal has been issued under subsection 570(5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "issued under this subsection"

-- 570 (6) If a warrant of committal is signed by a clerk of a court, a copy of the warrant of committal, certified by the clerk, is admissible in evidence in any proceeding.
-- src:12455 | (6) If a warrant of committal is signed by a clerk of a court, a copy of the warrant of committal, certified by the clerk, is admissible in evidence in any proceeding.
@ref s 570(6) (src:12455-12455)
GIVEN `the warrant of committal is signed by a clerk of a court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy of the warrant of committal is certified by the clerk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 570(6) a copy of the warrant of committal, certified by the clerk, is admissible in evidence in any proceeding` MEANS
    IF `the warrant of committal is signed by a clerk of a court` AND `the copy of the warrant of committal is certified by the clerk`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a warrant of committal is signed by a clerk of a court, a copy of the warrant of committal, certified by the clerk"

§§ `Sections 571 and 572 -- Adjournment; application of other Parts`

-- 571 (1) A judge or provincial court judge acting under this Part may from time to time adjourn a trial until it is finally terminated.
-- src:12457 | 571 (1) A judge or provincial court judge acting under this Part may from time to time adjourn a trial until it is finally terminated.
@ref s 571(1) (src:12457-12457)
GIVEN `the judge or provincial court judge is acting under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trial is finally terminated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 571(1) a judge or provincial court judge acting under this Part may adjourn a trial from time to time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the judge or provincial court judge is acting under this Part` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A judge or provincial court judge acting under this Part"
        IF `the trial is finally terminated` THEN JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until it is finally terminated"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 571 (2) In deciding whether to adjourn the trial, the judge or provincial court judge shall consider the interests of justice, including the interests of any victim of the offence in question if information related to the victim's interests is readily available.
-- src:12459 | (2) In deciding whether to adjourn the trial, the judge or provincial court judge shall consider the interests of justice, including the interests of any victim of the offence in question if information related to the victim’s interests is readily available.
@ref s 571(2) (src:12459-12459)
GIVEN `the judge or provincial court judge is deciding whether to adjourn the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 571(2) the judge or provincial court judge shall consider the interests of justice` MEANS
    IF `the judge or provincial court judge is deciding whether to adjourn the trial`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In deciding whether to adjourn the trial"

-- src:12459 | (2) In deciding whether to adjourn the trial, the judge or provincial court judge shall consider the interests of justice, including the interests of any victim of the offence in question if information related to the victim’s interests is readily available.
@ref s 571(2) (src:12459-12459)
GIVEN `the judge or provincial court judge is deciding whether to adjourn the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `information related to the victim's interests is readily available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 571(2) the judge or provincial court judge shall consider the interests of any victim of the offence in question` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the judge or provincial court judge is deciding whether to adjourn the trial` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In deciding whether to adjourn the trial"
        IF NOT `information related to the victim's interests is readily available` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if information related to the victim"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 572 The provisions of Part XVI, the provisions of Part XVIII relating to transmission of the record by a provincial court judge where he holds a preliminary inquiry, and the provisions of Parts XX and XXIII, in so far as they are not inconsistent with this Part,
-- apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to proceedings under this Part. (Part XVI is sections 493 to 529.5, Part XX sections 574 to 672 and Part XXIII sections 716 to 751.1, by the headings of the text.)
-- src:12461 | 572 The provisions of Part XVI, the provisions of Part XVIII relating to transmission of the record by a provincial court judge where he holds a preliminary inquiry, and the provisions of Parts XX and XXIII, in so far as they are not inconsistent with this Part, apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to proceedings under this Part.
@ref s 572 (src:12461-12461)
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the proceedings are proceedings under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is inconsistent with this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision of Part XVIII relates to transmission of the record by a provincial court judge where the judge holds a preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 572 the provision applies to the proceedings under this Part` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings are proceedings under this Part` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to proceedings under this Part"
        IF NOT (`in Part XVI` OR `in Part XVIII, in the transmission limb` OR `in Part XX` OR `in Part XXIII`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provisions of Part XVI, the provisions of Part XVIII relating to transmission of the record by a provincial court judge where he holds a preliminary inquiry, and the provisions of Parts XX and XXIII"
        IF `the provision is inconsistent with this Part` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in so far as they are not inconsistent with this Part"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `in Part XVI` MEANS `the provision`'s `section` AT LEAST 493 AND `the provision`'s `section` AT MOST 529.5
        `in Part XVIII, in the transmission limb` MEANS `the provision`'s `section` AT LEAST 535 AND `the provision`'s `section` AT MOST 551 AND `the provision of Part XVIII relates to transmission of the record by a provincial court judge where the judge holds a preliminary inquiry`
        `in Part XX` MEANS `the provision`'s `section` AT LEAST 574 AND `the provision`'s `section` AT MOST 672
        `in Part XXIII` MEANS `the provision`'s `section` AT LEAST 716 AND `the provision`'s `section` AT MOST 751.1
